1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,210
In 1960, three scientists calculated the end of the world:
1960年，三位科学家算出了世界末日：

2
00:00:04,210 --> 00:00:06,620
Friday, November thirteenth, 2026.
2026年11月13日，星期五。

3
00:00:06,620 --> 00:00:08,320
That is eleven days from today.
那是十一天以后。

4
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:10,140
Yes, I checked my calendar too.
对，我也去翻了日历。

5
00:00:10,140 --> 00:00:11,810
They published it in Science,
论文登在《科学》上，

6
00:00:11,810 --> 00:00:13,830
one of the top journals on Earth.
世界顶级的期刊。

7
00:00:13,830 --> 00:00:15,080
Their claim: on that day,
他们说，到那一天，

8
00:00:15,080 --> 00:00:17,190
the number of humans shoots to infinity.
人口会冲向无穷大。

9
00:00:17,190 --> 00:00:19,680
They wrote: our great great grand kids will not starve.
他们写道：我们的玄孙不会饿死，

10
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:21,200
They will be squeezed to death.
会被挤死。

11
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:23,140
Time magazine and The New York Times
《时代》周刊和《纽约时报》

12
00:00:23,140 --> 00:00:23,850
covered it.
都报道了它。

13
00:00:23,850 --> 00:00:25,000
Today's brain teaser:
今天的烧脑问题：

14
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:27,700
how can math put infinity on a specific Friday?
数学怎么能算出一个“无穷大”的星期五？

15
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:29,890
Start with normal growth, exponential,
先说普通的增长：指数增长，

16
00:00:29,890 --> 00:00:31,220
like money in a bank.
就像存在银行里的钱。

17
00:00:31,220 --> 00:00:33,790
Exponential growth has a fixed doubling time,
指数增长的翻倍时间是固定的，

18
00:00:33,790 --> 00:00:35,620
say, double every forty years.
比如每四十年翻一倍。

19
00:00:35,620 --> 00:00:36,330
It gets huge,
它会变得很大，

20
00:00:36,330 --> 00:00:38,100
but it never reaches infinity.
但永远到不了无穷。

21
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:40,040
Twist one: they found that humans grew
反转一：他们发现，人类长得

22
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:41,400
faster than exponential.
比指数还快。

23
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:43,180
They checked twenty four estimates
他们查了两千年里

24
00:00:43,180 --> 00:00:45,730
of world population across two thousand years.
二十四个世界人口估计。

25
00:00:45,730 --> 00:00:46,740
And the doubling time
翻倍的时间，

26
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:47,870
kept getting shorter.
越来越短。

27
00:00:47,870 --> 00:00:50,140
Their idea: more people means more ideas,
他们的想法：人越多，点子越多，

28
00:00:50,140 --> 00:00:51,640
more teamwork, more food.
合作越多，粮食越多。

29
00:00:51,640 --> 00:00:53,220
So growth feeds on itself,
于是增长喂养增长，

30
00:00:53,220 --> 00:00:54,440
faster and faster.
越来越快。

31
00:00:54,440 --> 00:00:56,450
Bacteria in a dish do not do that.
培养皿里的细菌可不会这样，

32
00:00:56,450 --> 00:00:57,930
They do not swap ideas.
它们不交换点子。

33
00:00:57,930 --> 00:00:59,830
Math calls this hyperbolic growth.
数学上这叫双曲增长。

34
00:00:59,830 --> 00:01:00,960
Here is the trick.
诀窍在这儿。

35
00:01:00,960 --> 00:01:03,880
Picture each doubling taking half as long as the last:
想象每次翻倍，只用上次一半的时间：

36
00:01:03,880 --> 00:01:06,490
forty years, then twenty, then ten, then five.
四十年，二十年，十年，五年。

37
00:01:06,490 --> 00:01:07,050
Add them up,
把它们加起来，

38
00:01:07,050 --> 00:01:08,820
and you hit a wall at eighty years.
八十年就撞墙。

39
00:01:08,820 --> 00:01:09,820
Infinite doublings,
无穷多次翻倍，

40
00:01:09,820 --> 00:01:11,410
squeezed into a finite time.
塞进有限的时间里。

41
00:01:11,410 --> 00:01:13,450
It is a bit like Zeno's paradox,
这有点像芝诺悖论，

42
00:01:13,450 --> 00:01:14,530
run in reverse.
只不过倒过来用。

43
00:01:14,530 --> 00:01:16,390
That wall is a date on the calendar.
那堵墙是日历上的一天。

44
00:01:16,390 --> 00:01:17,750
They called it doomsday.
他们管它叫末日。

45
00:01:17,750 --> 00:01:19,320
Their formula pointed
他们的公式指向

46
00:01:19,320 --> 00:01:20,720
to November 2026.
2026年11月。

47
00:01:20,720 --> 00:01:21,930
Twist two: for decades,
反转二：好几十年里，

48
00:01:21,930 --> 00:01:23,740
the formula worked scarily well.
这个公式准得吓人。

49
00:01:23,740 --> 00:01:25,010
Until about 1993,
直到大约1993年，

50
00:01:25,010 --> 00:01:27,300
real numbers kept up with it.
真实人口一直跟着它走。

51
00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:29,050
Then reality fell behind.
然后，现实掉队了。

52
00:01:29,050 --> 00:01:29,940
Way behind.
掉得很远。

53
00:01:29,940 --> 00:01:32,180
Today there are about eight billion of us.
今天地球上大约八十多亿人。

54
00:01:32,180 --> 00:01:33,850
Not infinity. Not even close.
不是无穷，差得远。

55
00:01:33,850 --> 00:01:35,260
Run their formula for today,
按他们的公式算，

56
00:01:35,260 --> 00:01:37,630
and you get about two hundred billion people.
今天地球上该有大约两千亿人。

57
00:01:37,630 --> 00:01:38,920
Twist three, the weirdest:
反转三，最奇妙：

58
00:01:38,920 --> 00:01:41,320
maybe the warning helped break the prediction.
也许是警告本身，打破了预言。

59
00:01:41,320 --> 00:01:42,390
Their cure was to cut
他们开的药方是：

60
00:01:42,390 --> 00:01:44,000
the world birth rate in half.
把全世界的出生率减半。

61
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:45,740
Today the global birth rate is
今天全球出生率

62
00:01:45,740 --> 00:01:48,120
slightly less than half its 1960 level.
比1960年的一半还略低一点。

63
00:01:48,120 --> 00:01:49,790
Of course, many things drove that:
当然原因很多：

64
00:01:49,790 --> 00:01:51,970
medicine, school, cities, family planning.
医疗、上学、进城、计划生育。

65
00:01:51,970 --> 00:01:53,310
Physicists know the sign:
物理学家都懂这个信号：

66
00:01:53,310 --> 00:01:56,200
when a formula hits infinity, the model is breaking.
公式一算出无穷，模型就要坏了。

67
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:57,300
Something it ignored,
它忽略的东西，

68
00:01:57,300 --> 00:02:00,020
like food, space, or people's choices, takes over.
比如粮食、空间、人的选择，会接管一切。

69
00:02:00,020 --> 00:02:01,000
Real growth curves
真实的增长曲线，

70
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:02,260
bend into an S shape.
会弯成一个S形。

71
00:02:02,260 --> 00:02:03,700
Like rabbits on an island:
就像岛上的兔子：

72
00:02:03,700 --> 00:02:05,870
a boom first, then the food runs out.
先猛涨，然后吃的不够了。

73
00:02:05,870 --> 00:02:07,950
Critics in 1960 called the paper
1960年就有批评者说这篇论文

74
00:02:07,950 --> 00:02:10,220
ridiculous and manifestly absurd.
荒唐、明显荒谬。

75
00:02:10,220 --> 00:02:11,620
But it left a great lesson:
但它留下一堂好课：

76
00:02:11,620 --> 00:02:14,490
a curve that fits the past can still fail the future.
贴合过去的曲线，照样可能算错未来。

77
00:02:14,490 --> 00:02:16,740
Fine print: the date was a math warning,
友情提示：那个日期是数学上的警告，

78
00:02:16,740 --> 00:02:17,980
not a real prophecy.
不是真的预言。

79
00:02:17,980 --> 00:02:20,930
The forty, twenty, ten example is our simple picture,
四十、二十、十年的例子是我们的简化示意，

80
00:02:20,930 --> 00:02:22,380
not their exact formula.
不是他们的原公式。

81
00:02:22,380 --> 00:02:25,100
So, will the world end on November thirteenth?
所以，11月13日世界会完蛋吗？

82
00:02:25,100 --> 00:02:26,940
No. The formula ends, not us.
不会。完蛋的是公式，不是我们。

83
00:02:26,940 --> 00:02:29,300
But if your subway is extra crowded that day,
不过那天要是地铁特别挤，

84
00:02:29,300 --> 00:02:30,810
you know who to blame.
你知道该怪谁了。

